## 5. Conclusions
In summary, a series of polyoxometalate-based bimetallic electrocatalysts with precise component and construction formulated as \(\mathrm{Fe_{x}C o_{y}M O F-P_{2}W_{18}}\) have been designed and constructed for effective e-NRR. The synergetic effect of \(\mathrm{P}_{2}\mathrm{W}_{18}\) and \(\mathrm{Fe_{x}C o_{y}M O F}\) results in a significant enhancement of the e-NRR activity in \(\mathrm{Fe_{x}C o_{y}M O F-P_{2}W_{18}}\) compared with that of \(\mathrm{Fe_{x}C o_{y}M O F}\) and pure \(\mathrm{P}_{2}\mathrm{W}_{18}\) . Catalyst FeCoMOF- \(\cdot\mathrm{P}_{2}\mathrm{W}_{18}\) shows the highest \(\mathrm{NH}_{3}\) yield rate of \(47.04~\upmu\mathrm{g}~\mathrm{h}^{-1}~\mathrm{mg}_{\mathrm{cat}}^{-1}\) , a Faradaic efficiency of \(31.76\%\) at \(-0.4\:\mathrm{V}\) (vs. RHE) and long-term stability compared with other \(\mathrm{Fe_{x}C o_{y}M O F-P_{2}W_{18}}\) catalysts. DFT calculations and in situ FTIR confirm the directional electron transfer from \(\mathrm{P}_{2}\mathrm{W}_{18}\) to \(\mathrm{Fe_{x}C o_{y}M O F}\) that results in the increase of electron density at the bimetallic-site, and further significantly enhances the electrocatalytic activity of \(\mathrm{Fe_{x}C o_{y}M O F-P_{2}W_{18}}\) for
